      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Employment Verification Letter Workflow\n\nThis workflow automates the process of generating an **Employment Verification Letter** in Google Docs, based on employee data from Google Sheets.\n\n### Steps\n\n1. **Verify Employment (Google Sheets)**\n   - Looks up the employee in the **Employee Information** sheet.  \n   - Matches by `Full Name` and `Email`.\n\n2. **Copy File (Google Drive)**\n   - Creates a copy of the **Employment Verification Template** in Google Drive.  \n   - The new file is named:  \n     `Employment Verification of {{ Full Name }}`\n\n3. **Update Document (Google Docs)**\n   - Replaces placeholders in the copied template with real data  \n\n4. **Download File (Google Drive)**\n   - Exports the updated document as a **PDF**.  \n   - This PDF is now ready to be shared with the employee or requester.\n\n---\n\n**Result**: A personalized Employment Verification Letter in PDF format, created automatically from Google Sheets input.\n",
        "height": 800,
        "width": 816
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        80,
        -672
      ],
      "id": "f12b6c46-9fd7-42a4-9404-b20ec537f7a8",
      "name": "Sticky Note1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Send Email and Verification Letter to the Requester\n1. Email is sent to the employee with the attached PDF.\n2. After sending, the Google Sheet row is updated automatically to indicate that the letter has been sent.\n",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 624
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
